The Docling worker downloads model files onto its models volume (they are never part of an
image; see src/text_extraction/documents/models.toml):
- Tesseract's tessdata_best models deu, eng and osd (tesseract-ocr/tessdata_best),
  Apache License 2.0.
- Tesseract's `tsv` output config (tesseract-ocr/tessconfigs, commit
  3decf1c8252ba6dbeef0bf908f4b0aab7f18d113), Apache License 2.0.
- Docling's layout model "heron" (docling-project/docling-layout-heron, revision main at
  commit 8f39ad3c0b4c58e9c2d2c84a38465abf757272d8), Apache License 2.0.
- Docling's TableFormer model, fast mode (docling-project/docling-models, revision v2.3.0 at
  commit fc0f2d45e2218ea24bce5045f58a389aed16dc23), Community Data License Agreement -
  Permissive, Version 2.0 (CDLA-Permissive-2.0).

The ASR worker downloads the files of one Whisper model onto its models volume (never part of an
image; see src/text_extraction/media/models.toml). Both are CTranslate2 conversions of OpenAI's
Whisper models (openai/whisper, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI):
- faster-whisper "small" (Systran/faster-whisper-small, revision main at commit
  536b0662742c02347bc0e980a01041f333bce120), MIT License.
- faster-whisper "large-v3-turbo" (mobiuslabsgmbh/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo, revision main
  at commit 0a363e9161cbc7ed1431c9597a8ceaf0c4f78fcf), MIT License.

The NLP worker downloads two spaCy models (German and English, one size: `lg` or `md`) onto its
models volume (never part of an image; see src/text_extraction/pii/models.toml), as the model
wheels of explosion/spacy-models, version 3.8.0, MIT License, Copyright Explosion. The training
data, as the models' meta.json states it:
- de_core_news_lg and de_core_news_md: the TIGER Corpus (Brants et al., University of
  Stuttgart; commercial licence held by Explosion), Tiger2Dep (Wolfgang Seeker; cited for
  reference, no code in the model), WikiNER (Nothman et al., CC BY 4.0) and Explosion fastText
  vectors (cbow, OSCAR Common Crawl and Wikipedia; CC0).
- en_core_web_lg and en_core_web_md: OntoNotes 5 (LDC2013T19; commercial licence held by
  Explosion), the ClearNLP constituent-to-dependency conversion (Emory University; cited for
  reference, no code in the model), WordNet 3.0 (Princeton University, WordNet 3.0 License)
  and Explosion vectors (OSCAR 2109, Wikipedia, OpenSubtitles and WMT News Crawl; CC0).
Presidio (presidio-analyzer, Microsoft, MIT License) and spaCy (Explosion, MIT License) are
installed with the extra `nlp` of the NLP worker only.

The ASR worker image (Dockerfile target `asr`) contains the shared libraries of FFmpeg n9.0.2
(ffmpeg.org, tag n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068), licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 3 or later, as built by BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds (release autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08, variant
lgpl-shared; the build scripts and the configuration are at github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds). The
licence text is in the image at /opt/ffmpeg/LICENSE.txt. PyAV is built against these libraries and
links them dynamically; no FFmpeg program is included.

src/text_extraction/media/asr_check.ogg and tests/media/corpus/speech_de.ogg are read from
Franz Kafka's "Die Verwandlung" (LibriVox recording, public domain); see
tests/media/corpus/SOURCES.md.
